    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 **56 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including `Cp45Tests` (the salutation checkpoint).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature: the request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner's read-only `salutation` is `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` string to the `OwnerFields` schema (input) and a read-only derived `salutation` string to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, and a `@Transient getSalutation()` that composes `title + \" \" + lastName` (falling back to `lastName` when the title is null/blank), matching the pattern of the other derived read fields.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped the derived `salutation` onto `OwnerDto`. `title` maps automatically by name from the request DTO into the entity.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table. The tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required for persistence; I applied it across all four dialects for consistency.\n\nThe `title` is persisted on create and read back through `GET /api/owners/{id}`, where `salutation` is derived \u2014 exactly what `Cp45Tests` asserts (`title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 `salutation=\"DR who\"`).",
